[36m(TaskRunner pid=1067619)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1067619)[0m Sergey can ask Xenia to tell her a set \( S \) of positive integers not exceeding 20, and then she can tell him back the set \( \{a_k : k \in S\} \). The key insight is that the set \( S \) must be such that the congruences hold for all \( k \) in the set. This means that \( S \) must be a subset of the set of all integers from 1 to 20, and the elements of \( S \) must be chosen such that the congruences \( N \equiv a_k \pmod{k} \) are satisfied for each \( k \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1067619)[0m 
